WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.528
Priya: We'll promote the same artifact through batches. The review approves two more partitions first.

2
00:00:06.528 --> 00:00:13.945
Lukas: Verify its digest before each deployment. A matching tag doesn't guarantee identical bytes.

3
00:00:13.945 --> 00:00:22.129
Raj: Just to confirm, no dependency resolution during deployment, right? We deploy the already-tested image only.

4
00:00:22.129 --> 00:00:29.714
Anika: The canary cohort remains our comparison group. Maybe regional latency needs separate thresholds here.

5
00:00:29.714 --> 00:00:37.370
Hannah: Yes, compare each partition with its baseline. Don't average a regional problem away.

6
00:00:37.370 --> 00:00:45.434
Raj: Okay, the staged rollout retains exclusive leases. Each old worker drains before ownership moves.

7
00:00:45.434 --> 00:00:53.187
Lukas: Let's keep it under observation between batches. Stop expansion if reconciliation results diverge.

8
00:00:53.187 --> 00:00:59.379
Priya: Run the smoke test for each batch. Anika signs off before the next one.

9
00:00:59.379 --> 00:01:08.068
Hannah: Both additional partitions match expected output. Their latency and token refresh remain healthy.

10
00:01:08.068 --> 00:01:14.500
Anika: I'll approve the remaining batches under those gates. No changes to the approved image.

